## Starter

Starter is a multi-user task tracker: people sign in, keep tasks with a status and a due day, and
administrators manage the accounts. It began from the Airness Spring Boot template, a generic beginning for
an application built on Airness with Spring Boot, Thymeleaf, htmx, Tailwind CSS with daisyUI, and
PostgreSQL. Replace this paragraph with the goal of the application it becomes.

- `README.adoc` explains the template to people. It follows `README-guideline-writing.adoc` and must pass
  `adocent lint README.adoc`. Its diagrams are draw.io PNG files under `.adocent/resources/visuals` that carry
  their editable source: edit them in draw.io and export them with the diagram embedded again.
- A local run starts with `cp .env.example .env`, choosing the two passwords the copy leaves empty, then
  `mvn clean verify` and `docker compose up --build`.
  `.env.example` sets `APP_DEMO_DATA=true`, so the first start against an empty database writes a
  demonstration team, whose accounts sign in with the administrator's password at addresses in the
  administrator's domain, such as `maja.kowalska@starter.local`.
<!-- @SNAPSHOT_ONLY_BEGIN@ -->
- Every build starts the local npm registry with `python3`, which serves `@airness/node` from the Airness
  artifacts installed in the local Maven repository, so `python3` must be on the path and the Airness
  version the parent names must be installed there.
<!-- @SNAPSHOT_ONLY_END@ -->
- The `identity`, `audit`, `language`, `web` and `failure` packages are the platform every application
  keeps: sign-in, roles, account management, the audit trail, English and Polish, and the failure page.
- The `task`, `home` and `demo` packages are the example domain, which an application renames or replaces.
- A component is a Thymeleaf fragment under `src/main/resources/templates/components`. Pages call the
  fragments rather than repeating daisyUI class lists, and a fragment switches between whole literal class
  names, because Tailwind writes only the classes it finds written out in a template.
